Intel(R) Arc(tm) Graphics (MTL) / predictive coding; 7,200 normal neurons plus paired error populations, 4,214,784 shared w/-w connections. Eight nonnegative motor outputs.
Integration: 8 steps/frame, activity h=0.04, weight h=0.02, eta=1E-05, reward eta=1E-05. One local weight update/frame.
Main eta = base eta * (1 + total pleasure - total pain). Totals use normalized learned signals plus primitive sensations. Propagation gain stays 1.
Drive inputs = total pleasure + total pain * held U(0,1); noise refreshes every 12 frames. Negative reward factors reverse local plasticity.
Total error = SUM(E^2), statistics only. No actor/value objective, replay, backpropagation, biases or least-squares reward shortcut.
